1
00:00:06,470 --> 00:00:13,250
To make a shade of green, a decorator mixes 6 tins of yellow paint with 4 tins of blue paint.

2
00:00:13,300 --> 00:00:18,610
For a small job, she wants the same shade of green, but with fewer tins.

3
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:21,640
What is the simplest ratio of yellow to blue?

4
00:00:21,690 --> 00:00:25,190
Pause the video and work it out.

5
00:00:25,240 --> 00:00:27,860
Split the tins into 2 equal groups.

6
00:00:27,910 --> 00:00:31,080
Each group has 3 yellow and 2 blue.

7
00:00:31,130 --> 00:00:35,720
So 3 tins of yellow with 2 tins of blue makes the same shade.

8
00:00:35,770 --> 00:00:39,230
The ratio 6 to 4 is the same as 3 to 2.

9
00:00:39,280 --> 00:00:46,640
Remember: the highest common factor of 2 numbers is the biggest number that divides both of them.

10
00:00:46,690 --> 00:00:50,890
The highest common factor of 18 and 24 is 6.

11
00:00:50,940 --> 00:00:52,900
A ratio compares quantities.

12
00:00:52,950 --> 00:00:54,710
Yellow to blue is 6 to 4.

13
00:00:54,760 --> 00:00:57,060
We write it with a colon.

14
00:00:57,110 --> 00:00:58,440
The order matters.

15
00:00:58,490 --> 00:01:00,900
Blue to yellow is 4 to 6.

16
00:01:00,950 --> 00:01:04,820
To simplify a ratio, divide every part by the same number.

17
00:01:04,870 --> 00:01:08,750
It is best to divide by the highest common factor.

18
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:09,560
Your turn.

19
00:01:09,610 --> 00:01:11,830
Simplify the ratio 14 to 35.

20
00:01:11,880 --> 00:01:15,410
Pause the video and try it.

21
00:01:15,460 --> 00:01:19,470
The highest common factor of 14 and 35 is 7.

22
00:01:19,520 --> 00:01:21,410
14 divided by 7 is 2.

23
00:01:21,460 --> 00:01:23,350
35 divided by 7 is 5.

24
00:01:23,400 --> 00:01:25,840
The answer is 2 to 5.

25
00:01:25,890 --> 00:01:30,570
Before you simplify, both parts must be in the same units.

26
00:01:30,620 --> 00:01:35,790
50 centimetres to 2 metres is 50 centimetres to 200 centimetres.

27
00:01:35,840 --> 00:01:38,460
That simplifies to 1 to 4.

28
00:01:38,510 --> 00:01:40,720
A ratio can have 3 parts.

29
00:01:40,770 --> 00:01:42,070
12 to 18 to 30.

30
00:01:42,120 --> 00:01:46,510
Divide every part by 6, to get 2 to 3 to 5.

31
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:47,300
Your turn.

32
00:01:47,350 --> 00:01:49,040
Simplify 6 to 9 to 12.

33
00:01:49,090 --> 00:01:52,570
Pause the video and try it.

34
00:01:52,620 --> 00:01:56,410
The highest common factor of 6, 9 and 12 is 3.

35
00:01:56,460 --> 00:01:58,330
Divide every part by 3.

36
00:01:58,380 --> 00:02:01,050
The answer is 2 to 3 to 4.

37
00:02:01,100 --> 00:02:04,350
A ratio also tells you fractions of the total.

38
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:07,150
In the paint, yellow to blue is 3 to 2.

39
00:02:07,200 --> 00:02:09,860
That makes 5 parts altogether.

40
00:02:09,910 --> 00:02:14,680
So 3 fifths of the mixture is yellow, and 2 fifths is blue.

41
00:02:14,730 --> 00:02:16,000
Here is the method.

42
00:02:16,050 --> 00:02:19,060
Step 1: put all the parts in the same units.

43
00:02:19,110 --> 00:02:23,370
If there are decimals, multiply to make whole numbers.

44
00:02:23,420 --> 00:02:27,870
Step 2: find the highest common factor of all the parts.

45
00:02:27,920 --> 00:02:30,710
Step 3: divide every part by it.

46
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:31,770
Step 4: check.

47
00:02:31,820 --> 00:02:35,340
The only common factor left should be 1.

48
00:02:35,390 --> 00:02:38,080
Simplify 56 to 42.

49
00:02:38,130 --> 00:02:42,800
The highest common factor of 56 and 42 is 14.

50
00:02:42,850 --> 00:02:45,030
56 divided by 14 is 4.

51
00:02:45,080 --> 00:02:47,260
42 divided by 14 is 3.

52
00:02:47,310 --> 00:02:49,940
The answer is 4 to 3.

53
00:02:49,990 --> 00:02:53,920
Simplify 600 grams to 1.5 kilograms.

54
00:02:53,970 --> 00:02:56,110
First use the same units.

55
00:02:56,160 --> 00:02:59,210
1.5 kilograms is 1,500 grams.

56
00:02:59,260 --> 00:03:01,350
Divide both parts by 300.

57
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:03,700
The answer is 2 to 5.

58
00:03:03,750 --> 00:03:06,310
Simplify 1.2 to 3.

59
00:03:06,360 --> 00:03:11,880
Multiply both parts by 10, to get whole numbers: 12 to 30.

60
00:03:11,930 --> 00:03:14,010
Then divide both parts by 6.

61
00:03:14,060 --> 00:03:16,160
The answer is 2 to 5.

62
00:03:16,210 --> 00:03:17,610
Simplify 36 to 48.

63
00:03:17,660 --> 00:03:19,390
Here is Eva's working.

64
00:03:19,440 --> 00:03:22,210
Which line goes wrong first?

65
00:03:22,260 --> 00:03:23,500
Line 2 is wrong.

66
00:03:23,550 --> 00:03:26,240
The ratio is not fully simplified.

67
00:03:26,290 --> 00:03:30,100
18 and 24 can both still be divided by 6.

68
00:03:30,150 --> 00:03:34,800
Divide by the highest common factor, 12, straight away.

69
00:03:34,850 --> 00:03:36,980
36 to 48 is 3 to 4.

70
00:03:37,030 --> 00:03:40,240
You are watching this video in a ratio.

71
00:03:40,290 --> 00:03:45,820
A Full HD screen is 1,920 pixels wide and 1,080 pixels high.

72
00:03:45,870 --> 00:03:49,050
Divide both by 120, and you get 16 to 9.

73
00:03:49,100 --> 00:03:52,840
That is the shape of most screens today.

74
00:03:52,890 --> 00:03:58,350
On a bicycle, a front gear with 48 teeth drives a back gear with 16 teeth.

75
00:03:58,400 --> 00:04:00,280
That is a ratio of 3 to 1.

76
00:04:00,330 --> 00:04:04,330
One turn of the pedals turns the wheel 3 times.

77
00:04:04,380 --> 00:04:05,740
One last question.

78
00:04:05,790 --> 00:04:08,720
Simplify 80 centimetres to 1.2 metres.

79
00:04:08,770 --> 00:04:12,620
Pause the video and work it out.

80
00:04:12,670 --> 00:04:14,420
Use the same units.

81
00:04:14,470 --> 00:04:17,260
1.2 metres is 120 centimetres.

82
00:04:17,310 --> 00:04:20,000
80 to 120: divide both by 40.

83
00:04:20,050 --> 00:04:22,540
The answer is 2 to 3.

84
00:04:22,590 --> 00:04:27,070
To remember: a ratio compares quantities, in a fixed order.

85
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:31,900
Simplify by dividing every part by the highest common factor.

86
00:04:31,950 --> 00:04:34,620
Use the same units in every part.

87
00:04:34,670 --> 00:04:38,080
Add the parts to find fractions of the total.

88
00:04:38,130 --> 00:04:43,470
Great work! Now practise lesson 12.1 on Camday.
